00:16:50.592 --> 00:16:52.094
Why? Are you guys okay?

260
00:16:52.136 --> 00:16:55.806
Not really.
Tech's invaded our house too.

261
00:16:55.848 --> 00:16:56.724
Oh. no.

262
00:16:56.765 --> 00:16:58.392
Yeah. her name's Lilypad.

263
00:16:58.517 --> 00:17:01.103
Looks like a frog.
but really. she's a leech.

264
00:17:01.145 --> 00:17:03.313
sucking up
all of Bonnie's attention.

265
00:17:03.397 --> 00:17:06.608
Making her stare
at her screen all day.

266
00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:09.069
There's got to be
some way to stop it.

267
00:17:09.111 --> 00:17:11.113
I don't know. Jessie. Uh...

268
00:17:11.155 --> 00:17:14.158
Toys are for play.
but tech is...

269
00:17:14.241 --> 00:17:16.493
it's for everything.

270
00:17:19.121 --> 00:17:22.041
You remember
my first kid. Emily?

271
00:17:22.082 --> 00:17:25.586
The one I told you about
who gave me away.

272
00:17:25.627 --> 00:17:27.379
Course I do. yeah.

273
00:17:27.421 --> 00:17:30.215
It feels like that
all over again.

274
00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:32.926
First we were playing...

275
00:17:34.678 --> 00:17:36.055
...and then the world
started changing.

276
00:17:36.096 --> 00:17:38.223
I know.

277
00:17:38.265 --> 00:17:40.350
Emily changed and then...

278
00:17:41.268 --> 00:17:42.352
just like that...

279
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.564
my time with her was over.

280
00:17:47.024 --> 00:17:50.319
Now I'm losing Bonnie
to this device.

281
00:17:51.653 --> 00:17:53.572
Is it me?

282
00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:56.200
Am I just no good
at being a toy?

283
00:17:56.241 --> 00:17:58.202
Jessie. you're a good toy.

284
00:17:58.243 --> 00:18:00.579
- I don't know.
- Jessie.

285
00:18:04.958 --> 00:18:07.753
Okay.
Jessie...

286
00:18:07.795 --> 00:18:10.798
No. Sheriff... Sheriff Jessie.
I appreciate this promotion.

287
00:18:10.839 --> 00:18:12.674
but what I'd really like
to promote...

288
00:18:12.716 --> 00:18:14.510
No. that is so stupid.

289
00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:19.723
But she got Bonnie invited
to a sleepover in seconds.

290
00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:22.893
Jessie. you know
Bonnie better than anyone.

291
00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:24.478
What does your gut say?

292
00:18:30.609 --> 00:18:32.736
- That it can't be that easy.
- Mm-hmm.

293
00:18:32.778 --> 00:18:33.987
Bonnie won't click

294
00:18:34.029 --> 00:18:35.489
-with just anyone.
- Exactly.

295
00:18:35.531 --> 00:18:37.866
She needs to actually
meet these girls.

296
00:18:37.908 --> 00:18:41.662
She's not like most kids.
Bonnie plays different. She...

297
00:18:43.872 --> 00:18:45.833
She needs to play.

298
00:18:45.874 --> 00:18:47.835
- Jessie?
- You're right. Woody.

299
00:18:47.876 --> 00:18:49.545
Toys are for play.

300
00:18:49.586 --> 00:18:52.047
And play is how
she'll find the right friend.

301
00:18:52.089 --> 00:18:53.173
Okay.

302
00:18:53.215 --> 00:18:55.300
The age of toys may be over.

303
00:18:55.342 --> 00:18:58.303
but I'm gonna do something
useful before I go.

304
00:18:58.345 --> 00:18:59.805
I'm going to that sleepover.

305
00:18:59.847 --> 00:19:02.683
and making a real friend
for Bonnie.

306
00:19:02.724 --> 00:19:04.643
- Jessie. are you okay?
- Buzz!

307
00:19:04.685 --> 00:19:06.186
Jessie? Jessie!

308
00:19:06.228 --> 00:19:07.896
What do you think
you're doing?

309
00:19:07.938 --> 00:19:09.731
What are you doing?
I assumed you needed backup.

310
00:19:09.773 --> 00:19:10.941
No! I don't...

311
00:19:10.983 --> 00:19:13.694
Need backup. Deputy.

312
00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.406
- What happened?
- Why are we whispering?

313
00:19:17.447 --> 00:19:18.574
He's finally asleep.

314
00:19:18.615 --> 00:19:20.033
So what's wrong?

315
00:19:20.075 --> 00:19:21.994
I don't know.
but you heard Jessie.

316
00:19:22.035 --> 00:19:23.704
She needs a deputy.

317
00:19:23.745 --> 00:19:24.830
Machines!

318
00:19:24.872 --> 00:19:26.790
-Jessie.
-Yeah. what is it?

319
00:19:26.832 --> 00:19:27.875
Uh...

320
00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.753
You know...
Never mind. Never mind.

321
00:19:31.795 --> 00:19:33.964
If you need anything.
I'm here. At your service.

322
00:19:34.006 --> 00:19:36.091
Okay. Thanks.

323
00:19:36.133 --> 00:19:38.594
Come on. Bullseye.
I'm gonna need your help.

324
00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:02.284
We can't see the stars. Buzz.
Too much fog.

325
00:20:02.326 --> 00:20:06.121
Hmm.
We need to find higher ground.

326
00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:39.112
Huh?

327
00:20:49.331 --> 00:20:50.374
A-ha!

328
00:20:59.675 --> 00:21:02.302
Buzz. I have our bearings.
East-north--

329
00:21:10.644 --> 00:21:12.396
I'm not cleaning that up.

330
00:21:16.024 --> 00:21:18.527
-Why did we...
-Freeze?

331
00:21:19.069 --> 00:21:20.028
Fascinating.

332
00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:21.446
-Must...
-Avoid...

333
00:21:21.488 --> 00:21:22.364
Humans.

334
00:21:22.406 --> 00:21:23.615
Affirmative.

335
00:21:31.331 --> 00:21:33.083
Bonnie! Time to go
to your sleepover.

336
00:21:34.334 --> 00:21:35.252
Hmm.

337
00:21:37.087 --> 00:21:38.380
Um...

338
00:21:40.215 --> 00:21:42.676
Yo. Bonnie.
uh. what are you doing?

339
00:21:42.718 --> 00:21:44.553
You said you finished packing.

340
00:21:44.594 --> 00:21:47.306
Well. I did. but it's
my very first sleepover. Dad.

341
00:21:47.347 --> 00:21:49.349
I wanna be
extra. extra prepared.

342
00:21:49.391 --> 00:21:50.976
You're gonna be fine. sweetie.

343
00:21:51.018 --> 00:21:53.228
Come on. Go put on your shoes.
We got to go.

344
00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.354
Okay. okay.

345
00:22:00.027 --> 00:22:01.111
Jessie.

346
00:22:02.821 --> 00:22:03.822
Uh...

347
00:22:04.406 --> 00:22:06.074
What are you doing?

348
00:22:06.116 --> 00:22:09.536
We are gonna check out
these "friends" for ourselves

349
00:22:09.578 --> 00:22:11.872
and see if there is a real one
in the bunch.

350
00:22:11.913 --> 00:22:13.832
Okay. pause. It is not
a good look for Bonnie

351
00:22:13.874 --> 00:22:15.834
to bring toys to a sleepover.

352
00:22:15.876 --> 00:22:17.169
-I do. I do. I do.
-Deputy Buzz.

353
00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:19.588
I do!
I mean. I've done things.

354
00:22:19.629 --> 00:22:21.506
Make sure that device
don't take charge of anything

355
00:22:21.548 --> 00:22:22.507
while we're away.

356
00:22:22.549 --> 00:22:24.134
Yes. Sheriff. I'm on it.

357
00:22:24.176 --> 00:22:26.011
- All right. time to go.
- Okay.

358
00:22:26.053 --> 00:22:27.846
No. Jessie.
Get out of that bag.

359
00:22:27.888 --> 00:22:29.848
I'm only thinking about
what's best for Bonnie.

360
00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:32.768
Well. what do you know?
That's exactly what I'm doing.

361
00:22:40.984 --> 00:22:42.527
Did you pack your toothbrush?

362
00:22:42.569 --> 00:22:44.237
I think so.

363
00:22:45.697 --> 00:22:48.742
Oh. thanks. Dad. You packed
Jessie and Bullseye.

364
00:22:48.784 --> 00:22:51.536
Uh. did I?
Well. you're welcome.

365
00:22:52.871 --> 00:22:54.664
And here we are.

366
00:22:55.332 --> 00:22:56.875
Oh. oh. oh. oh!

367
00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:59.711
I wonder if Kara and Heidi
are here yet.

368
00:22:59.753 --> 00:23:02.422
Oh! Over there. Dad.
I see them. Park right there.

369
00:23:02.464 --> 00:23:04.424
Okay. okay. I see them.

370
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:08.053
Uh. Bonnie.
You forgot your bag.

371
00:23:09.388 --> 00:23:11.640
-Hey. Chelsea.
-Oh. hey. Bonnie.

372
00:23:11.681 --> 00:23:13.850
-Guys. you remember Bonnie?
-Hi.

373
00:23:13.892 --> 00:23:15.685
And this is Jessie.

374
00:23:15.727 --> 00:23:18.397
I ain't afraid
of nothin'. partner.

375
00:23:19.773 --> 00:23:22.651
Oh. You still play with toys?

376
00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:28.907
Um... Uh...

377
00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:32.202
Uh. um... uh...

378
00:23:32.244 --> 00:23:33.578
No. Be right back.

379
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:36.331
-Here you go. sweetie.
-Dad. take these.

380
00:23:36.373 --> 00:23:37.749
But I thought
you wanted your toys?

381
00:23:37.791 --> 00:23:38.959
Dad. just go.

382
00:23:47.134 --> 00:23:48.218
Guys.

383
00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:49.928
-I got my Lilypad.
-Bye!

384
00:23:53.223 --> 00:23:54.307
No.

385
00:24:19.583 --> 00:24:20.417
No. no. no.

386
00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:24.129
No. no. no. this is all wrong.

387
00:24:24.171 --> 00:24:25.714
How is she
supposed to make friends

388
00:24:25.755 --> 00:24:27.299
if they ain't even
looking at each oth--

389
00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:30.635
Oh.

390
00:24:34.973 --> 00:24:38.185
Oh. no.
Somebody lost their toys.

391
00:24:38.226 --> 00:24:39.352
What's that?

392
00:24:39.394 --> 00:24:41.855
I said
somebody lost their toys.

393
00:24:44.024 --> 00:24:45.275
Let's see.

394
00:24:46.485 --> 00:24:49.404
They belong to an Emily.

395
00:24:49.446 --> 00:24:51.698
Oh. and there's an address.

396
00:24:51.740 --> 00:24:53.909
That's not too far from here.

397
00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:55.535
We can drop them off.

398
00:25:04.085 --> 00:25:06.421
Turn right onto Ranch Road.

399
00:25:13.428 --> 00:25:15.180
You've reached
your destination.

400
00:25:16.723 --> 00:25:18.475
I'll just leave them here
in the mailbox.

401
00:25:18.517 --> 00:25:19.726
What's that?

402
00:25:19.768 --> 00:25:21.019
I'm leaving them
in the mailbox.

403
00:25:21.061 --> 00:25:22.562
-You're leaving me?
-Yes.

404
00:25:22.604 --> 00:25:24.439
No. no. no.

405
00:25:24.481 --> 00:25:25.941
No. no. no.

406
00:25:27.567 --> 00:25:29.778
No!

407
00:25:29.819 --> 00:25:31.655
We cannot be here.

408
00:25:31.696 --> 00:25:35.200
We've gotta
get back to Bonnie!

409
00:25:35.242 --> 00:25:36.576
Come on. Bullseye.

410
00:26:00.267 --> 00:26:01.935
Uh-oh! Uh! Oh!

411
00:26:01.977 --> 00:26:04.604
Whoa!

412
00:26:04.646 --> 00:26:05.981
Whoo!

413
00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:10.652
Hi!

414
00:26:10.694 --> 00:26:13.697
Bullseye! You thinking
what I'm thinking?

415
00:26:13.738 --> 00:26:16.032
Yeah!
Yeah. I'm gonna speak critter.

416
00:26:16.074 --> 00:26:18.118
and we'll
ride this horse home!

417
00:26:18.159 --> 00:26:19.953
We're coming. Bonnie!

418
00:26:19.995 --> 00:26:22.497
Yeehaw!

419
00:26:24.541 --> 00:26:27.335
Whoa. whoa. whoa!
Wrong way. horsey!

420
00:26:27.377 --> 00:26:29.212
Wrong way!

421
00:26:29.254 --> 00:26:32.549
Whoa. horsey! Whoa!

422
00:26:33.842 --> 00:26:36.511
No! No. no. no. no!

423
00:26:36.553 --> 00:26:39.264
Whoa!

424
00:26:51.568 --> 00:26:52.694
Bullseye?

425
00:26:55.447 --> 00:26:56.865
Oh!

426
00:26:56.906 --> 00:26:58.325
Thank goodness.
Come here. Help me.

427
00:26:59.409 --> 00:27:00.535
Daffodil?

428
00:27:02.871 --> 00:27:04.247
Geez. are you all right?

429
00:27:04.289 --> 00:27:06.750
Did something spook you?

430
00:27:06.791 --> 00:27:08.668
Come on. girl.

431
00:27:08.710 --> 00:27:11.129
Come on. Good girl.

432
00:27:13.715 --> 00:27:14.674
Hmm?

433
00:27:17.052 --> 00:27:18.553
Where'd you come from?

434
00:27:19.638 --> 00:27:21.348
He's perfect.

435
00:27:22.724 --> 00:27:25.435
No. Bullseye.

436
00:27:30.065 --> 00:27:32.567
Mmm... Hmm.

437
00:27:32.609 --> 00:27:34.569
Hmm.

438
00:27:34.611 --> 00:27:36.404
And how exactly will this help
us get Bonnie's attention?

439
00:27:36.446 --> 00:27:38.782
Well. when they come back
from the sleepover...

440
00:27:38.823 --> 00:27:40.575
-Careful. That tickles.
-...she'll enter the room.

441
00:27:40.617 --> 00:27:43.870
see Forky and Karen Beverly.
and remember the wedding.

442
00:27:43.912 --> 00:27:45.997
We are talking about
Bonnie. right?

443
00:27:46.039 --> 00:27:47.332
And not Jessie?

444
00:27:47.374 --> 00:27:48.792
Huh?

445
00:27:48.833 --> 00:27:51.252
Of course Bonnie.
Just Bonnie.

446
00:27:51.294 --> 00:27:52.837
Hey. what's everyone
talking about?

447
00:27:52.879 --> 00:27:54.756
Buzz is gonna
propose to Jessie.

448
00:27:54.798 --> 00:27:56.508
- Propose?
- Finally.

449
00:27:56.549 --> 00:27:57.884
Wait a minute. Wait...
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

450
00:27:57.926 --> 00:27:59.511
I didn't say that.

451
00:27:59.552 --> 00:28:00.929
-You didn't not say it either.
-Well. I...

452
00:28:00.970 --> 00:28:02.639
Who. Buzz?

453
00:28:02.681 --> 00:28:04.307
Question. Is Woody gonna
perform the wedding ceremony?

454
00:28:04.349 --> 00:28:07.143
I haven't thought
that far in advance. Forky.

455
00:28:07.185 --> 00:28:08.937
Okay. Then why is Woody
at the window?

456
00:28:08.978 --> 00:28:10.730
Woody!

457
00:28:11.606 --> 00:28:12.607
Woody!

458
00:28:12.649 --> 00:28:14.234
- Hey. everybody!
- Bo!

459
00:28:14.275 --> 00:28:16.027
Howdy. folks. Coast clear?

460
00:28:16.069 --> 00:28:17.445
The stage is yours. my friend.

461
00:28:17.487 --> 00:28:18.738
Woody!

462
00:28:18.822 --> 00:28:20.824
-It's good to s...
-Wow.

463
00:28:22.867 --> 00:28:24.619
Pretty cowboy.

464
00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:26.162
Why are you wearing
a dress. Woody?

465
00:28:26.204 --> 00:28:28.415
It's called a poncho. Forky.

466
00:28:28.456 --> 00:28:29.999
Thought I'd change it up.

467
00:28:30.041 --> 00:28:31.042
Yeah?

468
00:28:33.378 --> 00:28:34.546
Well. Bo likes it.

469
00:28:35.338 --> 00:28:37.674
It's good to be back.

470
00:28:38.341 --> 00:28:39.718
-Shiny.
-What?

471
00:28:39.759 --> 00:28:41.344
- Nothing.
- Love the poncho.

472
00:28:41.386 --> 00:28:43.012
Someone needs a brown marker.

473
00:28:43.054 --> 00:28:45.056
Wow. Look what Bonnie's done
with the place.

474
00:28:45.098 --> 00:28:48.017
It's...
She really let things go.

475
00:28:48.101 --> 00:28:49.018
-Oh. my.
-Oh.

476
00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:50.979
